{"kind":"assert","text":"Lanes from 15:30 EST, 10 November. This act adds to order act\nfc7576f8. Nothing in that order changes.\n\nOpen to the builder now. Each lane has its own subagent, worktree,\nbranch and promise. One full gate runs on the machine at a time.\n- F 2ad35350, G f682cbc4, H d49269fd and identifiers head (b)\n  a30f1b67, as before.\n- JP1 3c9a0f81: one invitation parser for Start, the CLI and MCP.\n- OPS-1 b380ea8c: the deploy command, the smoke check and the\n  runbook section.\n- OPS-2 7c9c00e4: the `dap` command as one installable package.\n- Read-only: the cutover family head plan 9ecd3efa, with its\n  fourth change in 710a5d76 (an ordinary application package).\n\nGate slot order when two lanes are ready: F, G, H, (b), JP1,\nOPS-1, OPS-2. A lane that owns a path of another open lane says so\nbefore it edits.\n\nNot filed yet: an archive for every room, and its drill. The\ncutover changes how the archive ref is keyed, so the generic\narchive driver starts from the new format after head (c+d). Three\ndecisions for it stand now:\n- All four Workers share one archive driver. Today only\n  worker.grow.ts wires it.\n- The drill for the stable base verifies a room from its archive:\n  `dap clone --archive`, then `artroom-replay --git --all`. No\n  restore command exists, and a restore is a later design.\n- A room with host `none` has no outside copy and stays outside\n  the drill. The operator page says so.\n\nCorrection to 710a5d76: docs/run-your-app.md:11 to 14 sends the\nreader to docs/cli.md for the cohorts that accept a package. The\nstatement itself is at docs/cli.md:243 to 257.\n\nPlanner work in the same period: documentation groups C, D and F,\nthe amendment of the Sequenced note, and the Live design note.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}